🐛 Bug
Hi, I'm seeing a segmentation fault with LibTorch if torch::arange is the first operation.
To Reproduce
Steps to reproduce the behavior:

Compile and run the following program:

#include <torch/torch.h>

int main() {
  std::cout << torch::arange(0, 3) << std::endl;
}
There's no segmentation fault if another operation comes first.
#include <torch/torch.h>

int main() {
  std::cout << torch::randn({2, 2}) << std::endl;
  std::cout << torch::arange(0, 3) << std::endl;
}
Expected behavior
No segmentation fault
